course: dictionary
lesson: 1025
title: Words joined together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A compound word is two smaller words joined into one. Bookkeeper is book + keeper. A keeper looks after something, so the parts give you a clue to the meaning.
explain: In business, a bookkeeper keeps careful records of the money a business earns and spends. «A bookkeeper records every sale and every bill so the business knows if it is making a profit.» Bookkeeping uses adding, subtracting and checking that totals match.
explain: Context helps you check your guess. The sentence tells you what the job is for, and the word parts tell you what it is built from. Together, they give you the meaning.
fact: A bookkeeper is a person whose job is to keep careful records of the money a business earns and spends.
fact: «Bookkeeper» can also be an old word for someone who looks after books.
fact: «Bookkeeper» is a compound word: «book» + «keeper».
fact: «Bookkeeper» has three double letters in a row: oo, kk, ee.
fact: An accountant is related to a bookkeeper: they check and plan the money, and usually have more qualifications.
exercise: «A bookkeeper records every sale and every bill.» What is a bookkeeper's job? | *Keeping careful records of money a business earns and spends | Cooking food in a busy restaurant | Driving buses to school | Writing stories for books in a library
exercise: Which two words join to make «bookkeeper»? | boo and okeeper | *book and keeper | bookie and per | book and keep
exercise: Find and copy the three double-letter pairs in «bookkeeper». | kk, ll, ee | oo, kk, rr | oo, pp, ee | *oo, kk, ee
test: What does a bookkeeper do with bills? | Hides the bills under the desk | Sends the bills to the school | *Records every bill so the business knows its totals | Throws the bills away
test: Which job is most like a bookkeeper's? | Someone who fixes cars | *Someone who checks and plans the money of a business | Someone who grows vegetables | Someone who paints houses
exam: «The old bookkeeper spent all day looking after the library's books.» What does bookkeeper mean here? | Someone who sells sweets | *Someone who looks after books | A person who drives a bus | A type of bird
